      "chunk_id": "PX-700_manual_v2.1.txt_2",
      "text": "pump load.\n \nFor PX-700 pumps, the normal bearing temperature should remain below 90 degrees Celsius.\n \nIf bearing temperature exceeds 90 degrees Celsius, stop the pump and inspect the bearing.\n \nSection 2: Vibration Alarm\n \nAlarm Code: VIB-HIGH\n \nPossible causes:\n1. Coupling misalignment\n2. Bearing damage\n3. Rotor imbalance\n4. Loose foundation bolts\n \nRecommended checks:\n1. Inspect coupling alignment.\n2. Check bearing condition.\n3. Inspect rotor balance.\n4. Check foundation bolts.\n \nSection 3:",
